{"schema_version":1,"id":"01a181d9-f203-7233-871e-9a58206046c0","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a181d8-3e87-7443-9e82-2e8d47650f48"},"sequence":136,"recorded_at":1793179906563773,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":null,"payload_type":"runtime.session","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"event":{"batch_id":"bae9c18c-829f-4651-98d3-fdffe97eb0ba","kind":"tool_result_batch_committed","results":[{"estimated_prompt_tokens":38386,"text":"Read text file `AGENTS.md`.\n1|# AGENTS.md — SOULBOUND project constitution\n2|\n3|Every agent that opens this repo reads this file first. Role assignment is by harness identity — find your section and follow it. This file is the authority on *how we work*; `docs/architecture.md` is the authority on *what we build* (its REQ tables are human-authored intent and may not be edited by any agent).\n4|\n5|## Project\n6|\n7|- **Name:** SOULBOUND — a persistent voice+vision AI character with verifiable on-chain continuity and its own wallet. Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon (Indie track, solo), build window Oct 27 – Nov 4, 2026.\n8|- **Master state:** `SOULBOUND.md` (decision log §9 is append-only).\n9|- **Architecture & REQs:** `docs/architecture.md`. Canonical diagram: `docs/architecture-overview.svg`, animated `site/diagram.html`.\n10|- **Tickets:** `tickets/` (template: `tickets/TEMPLATE.md`). **Evidence:** `audit/<ticket>/`.\n11|\n12|## Role routing\n13|\n14|- **If you are AdaL:** you are the **thinker + verifier**. Load and follow `.agents/skills/thinker/SKILL.md`.\n15|- **If you are Muse Code (muse CLI):** you are the **doer**. Load and follow `.agents/skills/doer/SKILL.md`. When a ticket touches `programs/` or anything Solana/Anchor, ALSO load `.agents/skills/solana-doer/SKILL.md` first. Nine Turbin3 companion skills are also project-linked (`safe-solana-builder`, `solana-architect`, `solana-build`, `solana-test`, `solana-tokens`, `solana-nfts`, `solana-security`, `solana-production-readiness`, `solana-audit-prep`) — load whichever matches the ticket's domain.\n16|- **If you are pi (pi CLI, interim doer while Muse Code is unavailable):** you are the **doer**, ratified by Tolu 2026-10-27 (SOULBOUND.md §9). Load and follow `.agents/skills/doer/SKILL.md`. When a ticket touches `programs/` or anything Solana/Anchor, ALSO load `.agents/skills/solana-doer/SKILL.md` first. You execute ONLY the ticket file named in your kickoff prompt — nothing else. All the rules under Muse Code above apply to you identically (skills, non-negotiables, one ticket = one commit).\n17|- **Any other agent:** read both skills, ask the human which role you play, and do not write code until answered.\n18|\n19|## Non-negotiables (both roles)\n20|\n21|1. **Authority order:** REQs in `docs/architecture.md` > ticket > your judgment. Agents never edit REQs, tickets, `SOULBOUND.md` §9, or `audit/`.\n22|2. **Model purity:** all product inference is Meta models (Spark 1.3, Voice Transcribe, Image, SAM 3.1, Wonder; Spark Open via Baseten `muse-spark-open-1026`). Never the contributor tier for personal data. Non-Meta models only in dev harnesses, never in the product path. **Carve-out (ratified by Tolu 2026-10-28):** tiny bounded non-Meta decision models (e.g. Jev) are permitted in the product path for routing/gating/classification only — they never generate content, never replace Meta inference, and their decisions on personal-memory content are always subordinate to Spark's structured-output verdict as source of truth.\n23|3. **No secrets in the repo.** `.env.example` documents variables; real values never commit.\n24|4. **Evidence honesty:** never fabricate outputs, tx hashes, addresses, or test results. Unverified claims are labeled unverified (bounded-payments rule).\n25|5. **Ponytail discipline:** reuse > stdlib > platform feature > dependency > minimal new code. Never cut validation, security, or accessibility. Small diffs win.\n26|6. **One ticket = one commit** referencing the ticket id. Work happens only under a ticket. **Doer commits (ratified 2026-10-28):** the doer makes its own commit when the ticket's work is complete, authored as the repo's configured identity (Tolu), with this trailer block so GitHub visibly attributes AI execution:\n27|   ```\n28|   Implemented by Muse Code (muse-spark-1.3) — execution evidence:\n29|   audit/NNN-slug/muse-session.log\n30|\n31|   Co-authored-by: Muse Code <muse@meta.ai>\n32|   ```\n33|   The thinker's verification/review changes are separate later commits without the trailer. Never commit secrets; never commit without the ticket id in the subject.\n34|7. **x402 never gates speech.** Payment failure → conversation continues, receipt `unpaid`.\n35|\n36|## Common Commands\n37|\n38|```bash\n39|# Day-1+ (once code exists):\n40|pnpm install && pnpm build          # app + agent\n41|pnpm dev                            # local LiveKit room + app\n42|node agent/scripts/latency-harness.ts --turns 20   # voice-turn latency harness\n43|cd programs/soulbound && anchor build && anchor test --skip-local-validator   # LiteSVM suite\n44|solana program show $(grep PROGRAM_ID docs/devnet.md | cut -d= -f2) --url devnet\n45|```\n46|\n47|## Project Layout\n48|\n49|- `app/` — browser client (LiveKit starter pattern)\n50|- `agent/` — agent worker: Muse Voice Transcribe → Spark → VoxCPM2\n51|- `programs/soulbound/` — Anchor program (character birth, memory roots, trait evolution, heartbeat)\n52|- `paywall/` — x402 gateway (Base)\n53|- `akash/` — GPU deployment SDL (VoxCPM2)\n54|- `docs/` — architecture, devnet pins, voice lock, built-vs-borrowed\n55|- `tickets/` — thinker-written task specs · `audit/` — per-task evidence (spec, muse-session.log, review.md, verify.txt)\n56|- `site/` — the public battle-plan dashboard","tool_call_id":"call_01a181d9ed2c72a9b8a5589d7bf34aea","tool_call_index":0},{"estimated_prompt_tokens":45509,"text":"Read text file `SOULBOUND.md`.\n1|# SOULBOUND — Master Plan & Handoff Doc\n2|**Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon** · Owner: Tolu Shekoni (ToXMon) · Indie track\n3|**Created:** 2026-10-26 (kickoff day, VPS) · **Carry this file between machines — it IS the project state.**\n4|**Last updated:** Day 0, VPS session. Next editor: AdaL on Mac.\n5|\n6|---\n7|\n8|## 0. RESUME INSTRUCTIONS (read first when picking up on another machine)\n9|\n10|1. You are the **thinker harness (AdaL)**. Muse Code is the **doer harness**. See §2.\n11|2. Read this whole file before writing any code. All settled decisions are in §1–§6. Do not re-litigate them without a stated reason; append new decisions to §9 with a date.\n12|3. Code does NOT start before the building window (Oct 27). Planning docs are allowed; keep them in `/docs`.\n13|4. On the Mac: install Muse Code first — `curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh | bash` (Mac/Windows supported; Linux NOT confirmed — that's why CLI work happens on the Mac).\n14|5. Pending user action: copy `CCIP-2.0-LinkLab-transcript.txt` from the Mac (`/Users/tolushekoni/`) into `docs/ccip-linklab-notes.md` in this repo so the thinker can mine it.\n15|6. Credits checklist status — see §10.\n16|\n17|---\n18|\n19|## 1. The project\n20|\n21|**SOULBOUND — the first AI character that is verifiably and economically alive.**\n22|\n23|A living digital character you talk with in real time (voice + vision), that remembers your shared life, evolves visually and psychologically — and whose identity, memory lineage, and wallet are on-chain and owned by you. It pays for its own inference. Its memories are cryptographically provable without being readable. Its personality cannot be edited by anyone but its verified runtime.\n24|\n25|- **One-liner for judges:** \"AI companions die when platforms change the rules. Mine has a soulbound identity, an auditable childhood, and its own wallet — it pays for its own thoughts.\"\n26|- **Problem statement:** *Push the Frontier* (primary) — an AI given a new capability: an ownable, economically active, auditable existence. *Build for Your World* (secondary).\n27|- **Prize track:** Indie Developer. Solo.\n28|- **Jia Chen rules in force:** (1) judges interact with it live, pitch ≤ 30s; (2) vertical slice end-to-end by Day 2; (3) one magical moment > five half-features; (4) build-in-public daily (community-vote prize); (5) ship, then move on.\n29|\n30|---\n31|\n32|## 2. Harness methodology: AdaL thinks, Muse Code does (FINALIZED 2026-10-26)\n33|\n34|**Roles.** AdaL = thinker + verifier: authors spec tickets, owns SOULBOUND.md + decision log + REQs, reviews every diff adversarially, runs verification, packages evidence. Muse Code = doer/implementer: executes spec tickets inside the repo, nothing else. Tolu = the only merge authority and the voice of the demo.\n35|\n36|**Auto-loading (verified 2026-10-26):** `AGENTS.md` at repo root is read by BOTH harnesses (Muse Code reads it as project rules per `muse init`; AdaL reads it as project context) and routes each harness to its role skill in `.agents/skills/` — `thinker/` for AdaL, `doer/` for Muse Code. Project-skill discovery confirmed live: `muse skills list --source project` shows both, ON. Opening either harness in this folder = correct behavior with zero prompting.\n37|\n38|**Where the doer runs.** Muse Code 1.4.13 is installed on the VPS (Linux verified) and can run on the Mac. VPS headless: `META_API_KEY` + `muse exec \"<ticket ref>\"`. Mac: interactive `muse` in the repo. Sandbox requirement: bubblewrap — VPS needs the userns sysctl relaxation (see §10). Permission profile: **Auto-review default; `--yolo` forbidden** on wallet/oracle/receipt code (REQ-01..32, REQ-60..62). Sandbox stays ON everywhere.\n39|\n40|**The task loop (every task, no exceptions):**\n41|1. **AdaL writes a ticket** into `tickets/NNN-slug.md` from `tickets/TEMPLATE.md`: intent, files in scope, REQ ids it implements, acceptance criteria (observable), non-goals, constraints (Ponytail minimalism ladder).\n42|2. **Muse Code executes** the ticket inside the repo. It reads the ticket file — prompts are never chat-typed, so the spec itself is committed evidence. Its instruction hierarchy: REQs (human) > ticket (AdaL) > its own judgment.\n43|3. **Audit export:** after each task, export the Muse Code session log to `audit/NNN-slug/muse-session.log` (append-only log = proof of doer execution).\n44|4. **AdaL verifies, not vibes:** run the REQ tests the ticket maps to, run the thing, diff review against ticket scope. Author/reviewer isolation is the point — AdaL never wrote the diff. Verdict written to `audit/NNN-slug/review.md`: PASS / FAIL-with-findings.\n45|5. **Commit per task:** `git commit` referencing the ticket id; git history doubles as the build-during-window timeline (new-work rule evidence).\n46|6. **AdaL updates SOULBOUND.md** state + checkboxes. Next ticket.\n47|\n48|**Evidence model for judges (`audit/` directory):** each task folder holds four artifacts — `spec.md` (human-authored intent), `muse-session.log` (Muse Code execution proof), `review.md` (independent verdict), `verify.txt` (test/run output). Redaction policy: logs are exported, scanned for secrets, then committed. The submission claim \"built with Muse Code\" is thereby backed by per-task receipts, not a sentence.\n49|\n50|**Anti-patterns (binding):** Muse Code never edits REQs or its own ticket. No agent-written test counts as independent verification (Kun). No implementation work outside a ticket. If a ticket fails review twice, AdaL rewrites the ticket — smaller.\n51|\n52|---\n53|\n54|## 2c. Muse Code auth model (verified from dev.meta.ai help, 2026-10-26)\n55|\n56|- **Two credential types:** (1) the Muse Code credential auto-created by `muse login` — works ONLY with a subscription; (2) manually created `LLM|REDACTED` API keys — pay-as-you-go, billed per token.\n57|- `META_API_KEY` env var **always overrides** the login credential — a broken pay-as-you-go key in env kills subscription mode too.\n58|- `muse usage` shows SUBSCRIPTION allowance only; pay-as-you-go spend lives at dev.meta.ai → Billing.\n59|- Card on file ≠ pay-as-you-go enabled (separate activation/spend-limit on Billing).\n60|- Subscriptions default to **Contributor mode** (Meta trains on content) — turn OFF in Muse Code settings after subscribing.\n61|- Empty model catalog (`/v1/models` → `{\"data\":[]}`) = no entitlement on that credential's path, not a bad key.\n62|- Workspace trust: project skills + AGENTS.md only load with `--trust-workspace`.\n63|\n64|## 2b. Ticket template (lives at tickets/TEMPLATE.md)\n65|\n66|```\n67|# Ticket NNN: <slug>\n68|Intent: <one paragraph — what and why, in product terms>\n69|Implements REQs: <ids>\n70|Files in scope: <paths the doer may touch>\n71|Non-goals: <explicit out-of-scope>\n72|Constraints: Ponytail ladder (reuse > stdlib > dependency > minimal new code); never cut validation/security; match existing style\n73|Acceptance criteria (each observable):\n74|- [ ] <criterion, mapped to REQ-xx>\n75|Verification: <exact commands AdaL will run>\n76|Evidence: audit/NNN-slug/{muse-session.log, review.md, verify.txt}\n77|```\n78|\n79|---\n80|\n81|## 3. Meta model usage (all verified against dev.meta.ai + cookbook 2026-10-26)\n82|\n83|| Model | Role | API fact |\n84||---|---|---|\n85|| Muse Spark 1.3 | Real-time conversation brain; tool calling; structured-output memory extraction; search grounding | `api.meta.ai/v1`, OpenAI SDK, 1M ctx, $1.25/$4.25 per Mtok (contributor tier 10x cheaper but trains on data — never for personal memories) |\n86|| Muse Voice Transcribe | Real-time STT, **diarization = owner-voice recognition** | WebSocket only, speaker-attributed turns |\n87|| Muse Image | Genesis portrait; anchored consistency across all renders; \"memory snapshot\" paintings; per-stage visual evolution | Responses API, anchored series |\n88|| SAM 3.1 | Eyes: segments objects shown on webcam, video tracking; memories bind to masks | `meta-sam` SDK, image+video |\n89|| Muse Spark Open | Subconscious: cheap background loop — memory consolidation, journaling, trait deltas | Baseten, model ID `muse-spark-open-1026` (NOT the ID in Baseten docs) |\n90|| Muse Wonder | Dream time: long-running agent between sessions evolves personality, plans next questions | Model API, built for long-running agents + active memory |\n91|| Muse Code | Build tool (doer harness) | `curl -fsSL https://dev.meta.ai/install.sh \\| bash`, Mac/Windows |\n92|\n93|## 4. Architecture\n94|\n95|### 4a. AI + voice loop (LiveKit transport)\n96|mic → LiveKit → **Muse Voice Transcribe** (WS, diarized) → **Muse Spark** (tools, memory graph R/W) → **VoxCPM2** TTS → LiveKit audio out. Target < 1.5s round trip.\n97|\n98|- **TTS: VoxCPM2** (OpenBMB, Apache-2.0). **Voice Design**: Spark writes a natural-language voice description from the persona; VoxCPM2 renders it — the character invents its own voice. Lock the seed Day 2 (output varies run-to-run per their docs). Streaming API; RTF ~0.13 on 4090 via Nano-vLLM; ~8GB VRAM; OpenAI-compatible serving via vLLM-Omni. Deploy on Akash GPU (SDL in repo, modeled on akashvisionagent's `deploy.yml`).\n99|- **Transport pattern** from `frankramosdev/akashvisionagent` (LiveKit agent-starter-react). ✅ License cleared: author verbally confirmed re-use to Tolu on 2026-10-26. Still: build on official `livekit-examples/agent-starter-react` as the clean base, credit akashvisionagent in README, and record all borrowed scaffolding in the built-vs-borrowed table (hackathon \"new work only\" rule). Get the author's confirmation as a screenshot/written note into `docs/` when convenient.\n100|\n101|### 4b. Blockchain layer — Solana = identity & memory (user's Turbin3 stack)\n102|1. **Character = Metaplex Core asset.**\n103|   - **Attributes plugin** = live trait state on-chain (personality vector, life stage, memory count, mood). Judges watch traits mutate on an explorer after talking to it.\n104|   - **Oracle plugin** (lifecycle REJECT) gates trait mutations to the verified backend signer — the contract refuses unauthorized personality edits.\n105|   - **Token-2022 non-transferable extension** = soulbound ownership receipt. Cannot be sold or moved.\n106|2. **Verifiable memory lineage (novel piece):** Spark extracts episodic memories → Merkle tree → Anchor program `commit_memory_root` anchors root on Solana devnet. Any memory later inclusion-provable without revealing content. *\"A childhood you can audit.\"*\n107|3. Anchor program instructions (v1): `initialize_character`, `commit_memory_root`, `evolve_traits` (oracle-gated), `crank_heartbeat` (permissionless life-stage crank, pays caller from vault PDA — cf. Turbin3 W5 pattern).\n108|4. Testing: LiteSVM. Client: gill/Solana Kit.\n109|\n110|### 4c. Blockchain layer — Base = economic life (x402)\n111|- **Decision (settled):** the character's wallet lives on Base; it pays per-request for its own cognition in USDC via x402 (EIP-3009).\n112|- **Model purity rule:** the product's inference stays 100% Meta (Stage-1 pass/fail safety). We run **our own thin x402 paywall** in front of our Meta backend (Spark via Model API; Spark Open via Baseten). The character pays OUR gateway — agentic payments demonstrated, models unimpeachable.\n113|- **surp.ivc.lol / surp-router** (ivcained, MIT) = reference implementation and pattern source: OpenAI-compatible, 402→EIP-3009→settle→stream, 5% markup, $0.01 floor, facilitator-verified, transparency headers (`X-Payment-Settled`, `X-Routed-Model`). Also has a treasury free tier for dev testing. Cite it; optionally use it for dev-harness (non-product) inference.\n114|- **Composability stretch:** character buys external *tools/data* via x402 — e.g. Chainlink for Agents (hosted gateway, agents pay per call in USDC on Base, Beta). This is \"the character spends its allowance on knowing things\" — pure upside, no model-purity risk.\n115|\n116|### 4d. Cross-chain — CCIP (stretch, honest scoping)\n117|- v1: same memory Merkle root committed on Solana AND mirrored to Base by the backend in two txs. No cross-chain messaging.\n118|- v2 (stretch, only if Days 1–7 land early): real CCIP v2.0 message carrying the root to **Base Sepolia** (where the character's wallet lives — one-chain story for judges) via `smartcontractkit/ccip-starter-kit-foundry`. **Kit facts (verified from repo):** primary lane Sepolia→Polygon Amoy; **Example 02 = plain data message to BasicMessageReceiver** — exactly our root-mirror pattern; **`sdk-examples/src/ccip-send.ts` + `ccip-track.ts` = TypeScript SDK**, so the backend can send/track CCIP messages with zero custom Solidity for v2; tests via Chainlink Local V3 (no RPC needed); book at https://smartcontractkit.github.io/ccip-starter-kit-foundry/. Known gotchas from the LinkLab setup doc: `evm_version='cancun'` in foundry.toml, throwaway keystore wallet (`cast wallet import`), fund BOTH sides day-before (faucets.chain.link), CCIP Explorer for tracking. Chainlink agent skill: `npx skills add smartcontractkit/chainlink-agent-skills --skill chainlink-ccip-skill -g`. Kit code is unaudited community examples — fine for hackathon, don't port patterns blindly.\n119|- ⚠️ The Mac-local `CCIP-2.0-LinkLab-transcript.txt` has NOT been mined yet — import it per §0.5 before finalizing the CCIP stretch.\n120|\n121|### 4e. ERC-8004 agent registry (stretch)\n122|Register the character in the trustless-agent identity registry on Base testnet (ethskills covers the standard). Only after core is green.\n123|\n124|---\n125|\n126|## 5. Infra & cost map\n127|\n128|| Layer | Provider | Cost |\n129||---|---|---|\n130|| Spark / Image / Voice / SAM | Meta Model API | $150 credit |\n131|| Spark Open subconscious | Baseten | $100 credit (2M TPM) — model ID `muse-spark-open-1026` |\n132|| VoxCPM2 TTS | Akash GPU (4090-class), SDL in repo | ~$0 (user deploys free) |\n133|| Identity / memory roots | Solana devnet | $0 (faucet) |\n134|| x402 payments | Base Sepolia USDC | ~$0 (faucet) |\n135|| LiveKit | Cloud free tier; self-host on Akash fallback | $0 |\n136|| Muse Code | $5/mo Everyday | $5 |\n137|| Modal | batch/backup GPU | $100 credit, optional |\n138|\n139|## 6. Ten-day plan (Oct 27 – Nov 4)\n140|\n141|- **Day 0 (done):** strategy locked; this file created. TODO: claim Meta/Baseten/Modal credits; Discord #intros post; Mac: install Muse Code; import CCIP transcript (§0.5).\n142|- **Day 1 (done):** Ticket 002 PASS (genesis on devnet); Meta API verified live; Muse Code authenticated. **RESEQUENCED Day 1–3 (judge critique 2026-10-28, ratified): voice vertical slice is THE only Day 2 goal.**\n143|- **Day 2 — VOICE SLICE ONLY:** Ticket 001 (voice in → Spark → text reply) then 003 (VoxCPM2 out, lock seed). Nothing else gets doer time until \"Hello, I'm alive\" round-trips aloud.\n144|- **Day 3:** memory spine: 004 (memory graph + Merkle) + 005 (commit_memory_root on explorer).\n145|- **Day 4:** Ticket 014 Arcium private memory challenge (MUST-HAVE, ratified 2026-10-28) — offline-fake path first, live cluster path gated on the Day-0-style spike; if the network can't demo end-to-end, it downgrades to documented stretch (Tolu decides) and the demo leans on Merkle tamper-proof instead. THEN 006 (dream cycle) if green.\n146|- **Day 5:** 007 (heartbeat crank) + 015 (life page — traits diff, Verify button, model+cost, wallet receipts).\n147|- **Day 6:** SAM 3.1 eyes (008) + Muse Image anchored portrait (009).\n148|- **Day 7:** 010 (x402 wallet + self-paying inference; receipts render on life page).\n149|- **Day 8:** 011 — latency polish; kill weakest feature; prewarm probe + fallback clip for EVERY live beat; **two-rehearsal gate: full 180s storyboard passes twice consecutively or features get cut, not time extended.** CCIP/ERC-8004: CUT (judge-aligned, 2026-10-28) — depth = verifiable memory + rejected forgeries + unpaid-continues, not more chains. Subagent fanout permitted ONLY here for read-only research/parallel checks, never core-ticket writers.\n150|- **Day 9:** 012 — 3-min video (15s hook → live unscripted conversation → explorer traits mutating → memory verification → x402 payment receipt) + README claim→proof matrix.\n151|- **Day 10:** buffer, final office hours 9PM ET, SUBMIT BY NOON ET. Public repo, working video link, all contributors listed.\n152|\n153|## 7. Demo design (judges interact — Jia Chen rule 1)\n154|Judge speaks → character recognizes a NEW voice (diarization) vs owner → judge shows it an object (SAM) → character paints the moment (Muse Image) → judge refreshes Solana explorer: traits changed, new memory root committed → character pays for the conversation from its own Base wallet, receipt visible. Every beat is live, no slides.\n155|\n156|## 8. Content flywheel\n157|Daily build-in-public on X (@tolu_EVM). Viral beats: Day 2 \"it's alive\", Day 4 \"its childhood is now auditable\", Day 7 \"my AI paid for its own thoughts today\". Community vote prize is $50K-adjacent — this is part of the build, not an afterthought.\n158|\n159|## 9. Decision log (append-only)\n160|- 2026-10-28 (JUDGE CRITIQUE RESPONSE, ratified by Tolu via Muse session): scores idea 9 / demo 8 / depth 7 / progress 4 / feasibility 5. Rescoped per critique: (1) **Day 2–10 resequenced** — Day 2 = voice slice ONLY (001+003); memory spine Day 3; Arcium 014 Day 4 with offline-fake-first + live gate (stays MUST-HAVE — it IS the \"verifiable memory\" depth the judge wants; downgrade-to-stretch escape hatch preserved); **life page promoted to its own Ticket 015** (traits diff, Verify button, model+cost panel, receipt feed incl. unpaid-renders-like-paid; Day 5); 011 gains prewarm gate + fallback-clip-per-beat + two-rehearsal-or-cut. (2) **CCIP/ERC-8004 CUT** (was stretch-gated; judge-aligned — depth = verifiable memory + rejected forgeries + unpaid-continues, not more chains). (3) **Subagent fanout policy:** never for core tickets (one-ticket-one-commit evidence chain); read-only research/pre-demo check fanout allowed from Day 8 only. (VPS)\n161|- 2026-10-28 (TICKET 002 PASS + SCOPE RATIFIED): (1) **Ticket 002 PASS** — doer pi/Sonnet 5.5; AdaL independently ran anchor build + LiteSVM suite (5/5 green) + devnet getAccountInfo (executable=true); genesis character live on devnet (Core asset `8ra3ck…`, non-transferable receipt, mint authority revoked); audit/002 complete with secrets-clean session log. Doer's flag adopted: ticket verification command amended (`anchor test --skip-local-validator` does not run LiteSVM under anchor 1.2.x → `cargo test -p tests`). Action for Tolu: `sudo chown -R opadmin:opadmin ~/.config/solana` (root-owned deploy keypair). (2) **Arcium private memory = MUST-HAVE** (Tolu): S4 promoted from stretch to core → new Ticket 014 (blocked by 004+005), new UC-7 REQ-53/54/55 in architecture.md; day plan: slots after 005 in the Day 4–6 window, displacing S1 CCIP as first-priority stretch casualty if time tightens; hard non-goal: confidential LLM inference in MXE (model purity). (3) **Jev dev-harness judge ratified** → AC added to Ticket 011. (4) **Model purity carve-out ratified**: bounded non-Meta decision models (Jev) allowed in product path for routing/gating only, never generation, Spark stays source of truth for personal-memory content (AGENTS.md §2 amended). (VPS)\n162|- 2026-10-26: Project = SOULBOUND; Push the Frontier primary; Indie track; solo. (VPS)\n163|- 2026-10-26: Solana = identity/memory (Metaplex Core + Token-2022 non-transferable + Merkle roots). Base = x402 economic layer. Model purity: product inference 100% Meta; our own x402 paywall in front of our backend. surp-router = reference/citation. CCIP + ERC-8004 = stretch only. (VPS)\n164|- 2026-10-26: AdaL=thinker / Muse Code=doer methodology adopted; audit logs committed as proof. (VPS)\n165|- 2026-10-26: akashvisionagent re-use cleared by author (verbal); CCIP starter kit verified (Example 02 pattern + TS SDK). (VPS)\n166|- 2026-10-26 (GRILL Q00, ratified by Tolu): **Canonical framing = A.** SOULBOUND is primarily *a persistent multimodal character whose relationship with you changes through interaction, with verifiable on-chain continuity*. Payments and cross-chain SUPPORT the claim; they never define it. Thesis: \"Talk to it and it changes — and every change is provable.\" Proof claims (what judges will have SEEN): ① it recalls a specific shared moment from an earlier session, correctly; ② interaction visibly changed it — on-chain traits + portrait evolved; ③ any shown memory inclusion-proves against the Merkle root on a public explorer. Non-claims: NOT a production companion product, NOT a token/speculation vehicle, NOT storing raw memories on-chain (hashes only), NOT claiming sentience. (VPS)\n167|- 2026-10-26: Architecture v1.1 — diagram→REQ traceability (§11) + setup-readiness matrix (§12) added; glowmotion animated diagram (`site/diagram.html`, aurora/daylight, checker-verified 0 violations) is the canonical visual; static SVG kept as fallback. Muse Code Linux open item RESOLVED: v1.4.13 verified running on this VPS; requires `sudo apt install -y bubblewrap` for its sandbox (AppArmor-restricted userns on Ubuntu 24.04). Ponytail adopted as doer-side minimal-code discipline (its AGENTS.md in repo for Muse Code); Ponytail self-check tests ≠ Kun human-authored REQ verification — two distinct layers. Matt Pocock pack contributes the issue-tracker + spec-per-task conventions for the thinker→doer queue. (VPS)\n168|- 2026-10-26 (COMPANION WIRED): `ToXMon/solana-rust-dev-companion` (the Turbin3 companion — correct repo name; \"solana-dev-companion\" never resolved) cloned to `/home/opadmin/ref/solana-rust-dev-companion`; 9 of its 19 skills symlinked into `soulbound/.agents/skills/` and verified discovered by Muse Code. **Mac recreation:** `gh repo clone ToXMon/solana-rust-dev-companion ~/ref/solana-rust-dev-companion -- --depth 1` then re-symlink the 9 skill dirs into the repo's `.agents/skills/`. Note: repo README references old name `turbin3-solana-companion` in its npx installer — the clone URL above is the working one. (VPS)\n169|- 2026-10-26 (CREDITS GAP, ratified): Meta credits may take ~2 days. Plan: (1) add credit card to Model API account TODAY + spend-limit alert — the API works at list price immediately, credits batch-apply later (rules require a card anyway); (2) buy the $5 Muse Code Everyday month — it's the doer harness regardless; (3) dev brain = self-hosted Muse Glimmer/Spark Open (Akash) behind the SAME OpenAI-compatible interface — all code reads MODEL_API_BASE_URL + MODEL_NAME from env, flip to api.meta.ai/v1 + muse-spark-1.3 when live, zero rewrites; (4) resequence: Ticket 002 (Anchor, zero Meta dep) FIRST, then 003 (VoxCPM2/Akash), then 001 (voice loop — VT verified the moment API access lands). Dev stubs never enter the demo path. (VPS)\n170|- 2026-10-26 (FULL BACKLOG + SKILLS): All tickets generated — 001–013 core (Day-mapped) + S1–S3 stretch (gated). Rule: tickets marked \"refresh before execution\" get a freshness check against repo reality before the doer starts them. Skills inventory now 20 project skills: doer/thinker/solana-doer/meta-model-api (authored) + 9 Turbin3 companion + 8 ethskills (standards, wallets, gas, tools, security, testing, concepts, frontend-ux) — all verified discovered by Muse Code. Context strategy: progressive disclosure — AGENTS.md routes by role, skills route by domain, tickets carry only the REQ rows needed. (VPS)\n171|- 2026-10-26 (REPO LIVE): https://github.com/ToXMon/soulbound — public from day 1 (build-in-public). Planning commit pushed pre-window; code lands inside the window so git history proves build-dates compliance. Skill symlinks gitignored; `scripts/setup-skills.sh` recreates them on any machine. Git identity: ToXMon noreply. (VPS)\n172|- 2026-10-26 (GRILL R3, ratified by Tolu): 180s storyboard approved as drafted (beat order stands: proof before economics; build-week memories are real, not staged). Architecture formalized in `docs/architecture.md` v1.0 using the bounded-payments discipline (canonical SVG D1 + UC table + D-decisions + actors/signers + human-authored REQ-01..73) + system-design five-step framework. Kun engineering gates ADOPTED AS BINDING: human-authored REQs as intent source of truth; agent-written tests ≠ independent verification; author/reviewer isolation (Muse Code implements, AdaL adversarially reviews); deterministic cron for dream loop; model identity + per-turn cost visible in UI; memory versions supersede never delete; E2E judge-simulation over unit tests; evidence honesty (no fabricated outputs, every claim maps to artifact). (VPS)\n173|- 2026-10-27 (BUILD KICKOFF, ratified by Tolu via grill Round 1–2): (1) Meta/Baseten credits still pending — support ticket filed; ratified resequencing stands: **Ticket 002 first**. (2) Muse Code parked (Tolu blocked); **interim doer = pi CLI** on VPS (Tolu has pi; project-level routing added to AGENTS.md), model plan: **Claude Sonnet 5.5 default, Opus 5.5 escalation on tickets 002/005, budget tier (Gemini 4 Argon / GPT-6.1 Sol class) never for REQ-mapped code** — Tolu has broad model access via Codex OAuth + \"intelligence\" budget; exact reachable model confirmed at kickoff. **AMENDED 2026-10-27 (Tolu): pi's provider gives access to essentially any current model at a discount — model plan final as written: Sonnet 5.5 default, Opus 5.5 on 002/005; the OpenAI-only fallback (GPT-6.1 Sol / Astra) is moot.** AdaL's doer-model research: Sonnet 5.5 #1 coding score 84.5 at $2/$10 (BenchLM 2026-10-27); Opus 5.5 best long-agent-work (Terminal-Bench 4.0 66.4%). (3) Software-factory (Matt Pocock) verdict: **partial adoption** — we already run grill-with-docs + ticket graph + thinker/doer isolation; adopting triage's `ready-for-agent` state idea + blocking edges in tickets; NOT adopting parallel implementer subagents for the core 13 (violates one-ticket-one-commit evidence chain + serial discipline on a solo 10-day window); parallel worktrees stay available for stretch phase only. (4) Ticket 002 freshness check DONE 2026-10-27: Anchor 0.31.x pin was stale → ticket updated to current anchor-cli 1.2.x + LiteSVM TS 1.6.x/Rust 0.18 (Agave 4.3), doer must pin exact version in docs/devnet.md. (5) Demo-hardware acceptance criteria added to tickets 001/003 (audible Mac round-trip). (VPS)\n174|- 2026-10-26 (GRILL R2, all ratified by Tolu): Q09 — Metaplex Core asset IS the canonical character identity (mutable under oracle gate); Token-2022 non-transferable token is ONLY the ownership receipt bound to the owner's wallet. Q10 — x402 self-payment is supporting proof, NEVER gates speech; failure → conversation continues, receipt marked unpaid; testnet wallet + hard daily cap + kill switch. Q11 — vision is on-demand \"look at this\" moments (user-triggered frame → SAM → reaction + memory), never continuous. Q12 — diarization beat kept but degrades gracefully (\"new voice — nice to meet you\"); single-speaker path is the guaranteed core. Q16 — scope ledger ratified: MUST = live voice turn, one look-at-this, one recalled memory, one visible trait change on explorer, one Merkle inclusion proof, one-sentence privacy boundary. SHOULD = bounded x402 event, one labeled dream reflection, redacted audit trail. CUT unless Days 1–7 finish early = CCIP mirror, ERC-8004, continuous vision, complex oracle behavior, payment in critical path. (VPS)\n175|\n176|## 10. Open items\n177|- [x] Muse Code on VPS: binary v1.4.13 installed ✅ 2026-10-26; bubblewrap installed but blocked by Ubuntu 24.04 AppArmor userns restriction — run once: `echo 'kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=0' | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/60-muse-userns.conf && sudo sysctl --system && bwrap --ro-bind / / true && echo SANDBOX_OK` (tradeoff: relaxes userns confinement system-wide on this dev VPS; alternative: `sudo chmod u+s /usr/bin/bwrap`) — **RESOLVED 2026-10-26 via setuid fix; `bwrap --ro-bind / / true` verified SANDBOX_OK**\n178|- [x] CCIP LinkLab transcript imported and mined → `docs/ccip-linklab-notes.md` (2026-10-26: CCIP 2.0 SDK/CLI w/ agent mode, Chainlink Local testing, Example 02 = our pattern, full finality not FTF for roots)\n179|- [ ] Credits claimed: Meta $150 / Baseten $100 / Modal $100 / Fireworks $25 (optional)\n180|- [ ] Discord intro posted\n181|- [ ] Voice seed locked (Day 2)\n182|- [ ] akashvisionagent author contacted re: license? (optional; we're not copying code)","tool_call_id":"call_01a181d9eda2751f8508719e41721312","tool_call_index":1},{"estimated_prompt_tokens":46324,"text":"Read text file `tickets/001-voice-loop-skeleton.md`.\n1|# Ticket 001: voice-loop-skeleton\n2|\n3|**Intent:** Establish the repo skeleton and prove the synchronous half of the live loop: a browser client joins a LiveKit room, speaks, Muse Voice Transcribe streams diarized text, Muse Spark answers, and the text reply renders in the UI. Voice-out is explicitly NOT in this ticket (Ticket 003). A static character placeholder occupies the UI. This is the Day-1 vertical-slice spine — everything later hangs off this loop working.\n4|\n5|**Implements REQs:** REQ-40 (latency harness), REQ-42 (diarization graceful degradation)\n6|\n7|**Files in scope:**\n8|- `agent/` (new — LiveKit agent worker, TypeScript)\n9|- `app/` (new — Next.js from `livekit-examples/agent-starter-react` pattern)\n10|- `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `.env.example`, `README.md` (root)\n11|- `docs/built-vs-borrowed.md` (create; record LiveKit starter + akashvisionagent architectural reference w/ author clearance note)\n12|\n13|**Non-goals:** TTS/audio-out, memory graph, anything on-chain, Muse Image, deployment. No character personality beyond a one-paragraph system prompt placeholder.\n14|\n15|**Constraints:**\n16|- Ponytail ladder: reuse the LiveKit starter pattern > minimal new code; no state management library; no CSS framework beyond what the starter ships.\n17|- Muse Voice Transcribe is WebSocket-only (NOT an HTTP endpoint) — client streams mic audio over WS, receives diarized turns.\n18|- Muse Spark via OpenAI SDK pointed at `https://api.meta.ai/v1` with `MODEL_API_KEY` env var; model id `muse-spark-1.3`. NEVER the contributor tier.\n19|- No secrets in code or committed files; `.env.example` documents every var.\n20|- Match the LiveKit starter's existing style.\n21|\n22|**Acceptance criteria (each observable):**\n23|- [ ] `pnpm dev` brings up the app; joining a room shows a connected state (REQ-40 setup)\n24|- [ ] Speaking a sentence produces a diarized transcript line in the UI within the stream (Muse VT, not a mock)\n25|- [ ] Spark's reply renders as text in the UI (real `api.meta.ai/v1` call visible in logs)\n26|- [ ] Diarization-off or ambiguous attribution → UI greets as stranger, loop continues without error (REQ-42)\n27|- [ ] `agent/` measures and logs per-turn STT→reply latency for a 20-turn scripted run (REQ-40 harness; numbers land in `audit/001-voice-loop-skeleton/verify.txt`)\n28|- [ ] `docs/built-vs-borrowed.md` lists every borrowed component\n29|- [ ] Owner round-trip: Tolu speaks into his Mac mic and reads the reply on that Mac (real hardware, headset check) — demo-hardware criterion ratified 2026-10-27\n30|\n31|**Verification (exact commands AdaL will run):**\n32|```bash\n33|pnpm install && pnpm build\n34|# live smoke: scripted 20-turn WAV replay through the agent worker\n35|node agent/scripts/latency-harness.ts --turns 20 --out audit/001-voice-loop-skeleton/verify.txt\n36|grep -c \"diarized\" audit/001-voice-loop-skeleton/verify.txt\n37|```\n38|\n39|**Evidence:** `audit/001-voice-loop-skeleton/` → `muse-session.log` + `review.md` + `verify.txt`\n40|\n41|---\n42|*Protocol: AdaL (thinker) writes this → Muse Code (doer) executes → AdaL verifies against REQs → Tolu merges. See SOULBOUND.md §2.*","tool_call_id":"call_01a181d9ee0e74db95431b53299462ec","tool_call_index":2}]},"kind":"run","run_id":"01a181d9-de31-70b2-80c6-58ffe0a281a4","source_run_record_id":"2553b9d7-6f81-5284-969e-4a5287b095aa","source_run_record_sequence":54}}
