{"schema_version":1,"id":"01a181da-48d9-7140-95ff-a059a10f63c4","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a181d8-3e87-7443-9e82-2e8d47650f48"},"sequence":373,"recorded_at":1793179928793860,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":null,"payload_type":"runtime.session","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"event":{"chunk":"Read text file `docs/architecture.md`.\n1|# SOULBOUND: Architecture & Requirements\n2|\n3|**Status:** v1.0 · 2026-10-26 · awaiting final ratification\n4|**Method:** bounded-payments doc discipline (canonical SVG + use-case table + design decisions + actors/signers + atomic REQs with tests) × system-design-skills five-step framework × Kun engineering gates × Jia Chen demo laws.\n5|**Canonical diagram:** [architecture-overview.svg](architecture-overview.svg) (D1). Flow diagrams D2–D4 are Mermaid, below — GitHub renders them natively.\n6|\n7|---\n8|\n9|## 1. Overview\n10|\n11|SOULBOUND is a persistent multimodal character whose relationship with its owner changes through interaction and leaves verifiable on-chain continuity. Judges interact with it live; every interaction can change it; every change is provable.\n12|\n13|| Use case | Component / handler | Signer / actor | Pass condition |\n14|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n15|| UC-1 Birth a character | `initialize_character` (Anchor) | Owner | One Metaplex Core asset + one Token-2022 soulbound receipt minted to owner; config PDA created; invalid input creates nothing. |\n16|| UC-2 Live voice turn | agent worker (off-chain) | — | Spoken question → spoken answer in the character's locked voice; first audio p50 < 2.5s warm. Diarization failure degrades to stranger-greeting, never to silence. |\n17|| UC-3 \"Look at this\" | agent runtime + SAM 3.1 | Owner / judge (explicit trigger) | One user-approved frame → mask → structured observation stored as a memory with provenance. No frame, no capture. |\n18|| UC-4 Recall + verify | app backend | — | A recalled memory renders with a Merkle inclusion proof verifiable against the current on-chain root on a public explorer. |\n19|| UC-5 Dream cycle | cron → Muse Wonder → runtime signer | Runtime signer (oracle-gated) | Between sessions: journal written, trait proposal produced, `evolve_traits` applies it on-chain. Non-oracle mutation is rejected. |\n20|| UC-6 Self-payment | x402 paywall + character wallet (Base) | Character key (policy-limited) | Each inference call settles USDC via EIP-3009 and logs a receipt. Payment failure NEVER blocks speech; receipt marked `unpaid`. |\n21|| UC-7 Heartbeat | `crank_heartbeat` (Anchor) | Anyone (permissionless) | Life stage advances when on-chain conditions hold; caller paid from vault PDA; early crank changes nothing. |\n22|\n23|---\n24|\n25|## 2. Non-functional targets\n26|\n27|| Target | Value | Notes |\n28|| --- | --- | --- |\n29|| First-audio latency (voice turn) | p50 < 2.5s, p95 < 4s | Warm TTS. Speech-to-speech; chain ops never in this path (C01). |\n30|| TTS cold start | eliminated | Akash GPU prewarmed before any judging session (C08). Three consecutive clean runs = readiness gate. |\n31|| Root commit latency | < 60s after session end | Fully async; user never waits on Solana. |\n32|| Demo availability | core loop survives: facilitator down, Akash down, Solana RPC down | Each has a named fallback (§9). |\n33|| Privacy | zero raw audio/transcript/portrait bytes on-chain | Only hashes/roots/traits on-chain (C02). Raw media session-scoped. |\n34|| Cost | < $1 per character-day at demo scale; hackathon total inside $150 Meta credit | Contributor-tier Spark NEVER touches personal memories (it trains on data). |\n35|| Demo scale | ~100 sessions/day peak, ~10 turns each | Sizing only; viral path discussed in §8. |\n36|\n37|## 3. Capacity estimation (back-of-envelope, before boxes)\n38|\n39|| Quantity | Assumption | Math | Result |\n40|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n41|| Tokens/day | 100 sessions × 10 turns × (1k in + 300 out) | 100×10×1.3k | ~1.3M tok/day → trivial vs $150 credit |\n42|| TTS GPU-hours/day | 15s audio/turn, RTF ~0.13 (Nano-vLLM) | 1000 turns × 15s × 0.13 | ~0.5 GPU-hr → one 4090 idles |\n43|| Solana tx/day | ~2 commits+traits per session | 200 tx | sub-cent total |\n44|| Base x402 | ~$0.01–0.05 per session | faucet USDC | negligible |\n45|\n46|Conclusion: no component needs scale engineering. Spend the complexity budget on **latency pipelining and failure behavior**, not throughput.\n47|\n48|---\n49|\n50|## 4. Design decisions\n51|\n52|| ID | Decision |\n53|| --- | --- |\n54|| D1 | The **Metaplex Core asset IS the character** (canonical identity; Attributes plugin holds mutable trait state). The **Token-2022 non-transferable token is ONLY the ownership receipt**. One identity, one receipt; they never compete (Q09). |\n55|| D2 | Raw memory content (text, embeddings, media) lives **off-chain**; only Merkle roots and trait state go on-chain. Any memory is inclusion-provable without revealing content (C02). |\n56|| D3 | **Sync/async split:** voice turn + minimal recall = synchronous. Portraits, trait mutation, Merkle commits, dream cycle = asynchronous. Only labeled-precomputed content is precomputed (C01). |\n57|| D4 | **x402 never gates speech.** Payment is supporting proof; failure → conversation continues, `unpaid` receipt (Q10, C05). Testnet wallet, hard daily cap, kill switch. |\n58|| D5 | Vision is **on-demand \"look at this\" only** — one explicit frame per trigger, never continuous (Q11). |\n59|| D6 | Diarization beat kept but **degrades gracefully**: ambiguous attribution → \"new voice — nice to meet you.\" Single-speaker path is the guaranteed core (Q12, C06). |\n60|| D7 | **Model purity:** every product inference is a Meta model. The x402 paywall fronts OUR Meta backend. surp-router is reference/citation only (Stage-1 pass/fail protection). |\n61|| D8 | **Human-authored REQs are the intent source of truth** (this document). Muse Code implements against them; agent-written tests do NOT count as independent verification (Kun: an agent-written test is a second copy of the agent's interpretation). |\n62|| D9 | **Author/reviewer isolation:** Muse Code (doer) implements; AdaL (thinker) adversarially reviews each diff against the REQ table before merge. Validation rigor matches stakes (Kun). |\n63|| D10 | The dream cycle is a **deterministic cron scheduler invoking Wonder** — never an agent relying on its own context to remember to dream (Kun: deterministic harnesses for repeated loops). |\n64|| D11 | The UI always shows **which model answered and what the turn cost**. Hidden model identity/cost = broken trust (Kun). |\n65|| D12 | Memory records are **versioned; corrections supersede, never delete.** A deleted-looking memory breaks the audit story. |\n66|| D13 | LiveKit transport; character voice is **Voice-Designed by Spark from the persona, rendered by VoxCPM2, seed locked Day 2** (VoxCPM2 output varies run-to-run per vendor docs). |\n67|| D14 | Scope ledger (Q16) is binding: CCIP mirror, ERC-8004, continuous vision, complex oracle behavior, and payment-in-critical-path are **cut unless Days 1–7 finish early**. |\n68|| D15 | TTS sits behind a **replaceable interface**; VoxCPM2-on-Akash is primary, a second provider is the documented fallback (C08). |\n69|\n70|## 5. Actors and signers\n71|\n72|| LOI category | Actor | Signs | Can | Cannot |\n73|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n74|| Direct actor | Owner | `initialize_character`, receipt holder | Birth the character. Talk to it. Trigger \"look at this\". Kill the wallet switch. | Mutate traits directly (oracle-gated), transfer the receipt. |\n75|| Direct actor | Runtime signer (backend key) | `commit_memory_root`, `evolve_traits` | Commit roots; apply oracle-validated trait proposals. | Move owner assets; mint receipts; alter history (roots are append-only). |\n76|| Direct actor | Character key (Base) | EIP-3009 authorizations | Pay the paywall within daily cap. | Exceed cap; transfer wallet balance outward; sign anything else. |\n77|| Direct actor | Crank caller (anyone) | `crank_heartbeat` | Advance life stage when due; claim crank reward. | Forge roots or traits. |\n78|| Beneficiary | Judge / visitor | nothing | Talk, show an object, verify a memory proof. | Write any state. |\n79|| Administrator | Owner (devnet) | upgrade authority | Upgrade the program. | Rewrite committed roots (append-only account structure prevents it). |\n80|| Stakeholder | Metaplex / Token-2022 / facilitator / Circle | n/a | Enforce their own program rules. | — |\n81|| Trigger | Dream scheduler (cron) | n/a | Invoke the Wonder dream cycle. | Sign on-chain directly (its output is validated by the oracle plugin + runtime signer). |\n82|\n83|**Trust boundary (explicit):** inside the boundary = Solana program state, Core asset + plugins, Token-2022 receipt, Base wallet policy. Outside = agent worker, all models, VoxCPM2, LiveKit, memory DB, paywall server. Everything outside is an **untrusted input**; the chain layer verifies signatures and roots only.\n84|\n85|## 6. Data flows\n86|\n87|**Write path (live turn):** audio → Muse Voice Transcribe (diarized turns) → Spark brain (tools: memory read/write, SAM observation ingest) → VoxCPM2 audio out. Post-turn (async): Spark structured extraction → versioned memory record → Merkle leaf → batch → `commit_memory_root`.\n88|\n89|**Dream path (async):** cron → Wonder reads memory graph → journal + trait proposal → oracle-plugin validation → runtime signer → `evolve_traits` → Attributes update visible on explorer.\n90|\n91|**Read path (verify):** app renders memory → computes inclusion proof against current epoch leaves → explorer link to the root commit tx → anyone re-derives the root off-chain and compares.\n92|\n93|**Payment path:** agent runtime → paywall 402 → character key signs EIP-3009 → facilitator settles USDC on Base → inference streams → receipt logged and shown on the life page. Failure at any point: speech continues, receipt `unpaid`.\n94|\n95|## 7. Flow diagrams (D2–D4)\n96|\n97|### D2 — Live voice turn (synchronous path)\n98|```mermaid\n99|sequenceDiagram\n100|    participant J as Judge/Owner\n101|    participant LK as LiveKit\n102|    participant VT as Muse Voice Transcribe\n103|    participant BR as Spark 1.3 Brain\n104|    participant MG as Memory Graph\n105|    participant TT as VoxCPM2 (Akash)\n106|    J->>LK: speaks (mic)\n107|    LK->>VT: audio stream (WS)\n108|    VT->>BR: diarized turn text\n109|    BR->>MG: recall (minimal, sync)\n110|    MG-->>BR: context\n111|    BR->>TT: response text (sentence-streamed)\n112|    TT-->>LK: audio chunks\n113|    LK-->>J: character speaks (p50 < 2.5s)\n114|    Note over BR,MG: post-turn, ASYNC: extract → leaf → batch\n115|```\n116|\n117|### D3 — Memory lineage + dream cycle (async)\n118|```mermaid\n119|flowchart LR\n120|    T[session turns] --> E[Spark structured extraction]\n121|    E --> R[versioned memory record<br/>supersede, never delete]\n122|    R --> L[Merkle leaf = hash]\n123|    L --> B[epoch batcher]\n124|    B -->|commit_memory_root| P[(Solana Anchor program)]\n125|    CRON[cron scheduler] --> W[Muse Wonder dream cycle]\n126|    W --> R\n127|    W --> TP[trait proposal]\n128|    TP --> OG{oracle plugin}\n129|    OG -->|validated| EV[evolve_traits → Attributes on Core asset]\n130|    OG -->|rejected| X[nothing happens]\n131|```\n132|\n133|### D4 — Self-payment (x402, Base)\n134|```mermaid\n135|sequenceDiagram\n136|    participant A as Agent runtime\n137|    participant P as Our x402 paywall\n138|    participant W as Character wallet (Base)\n139|    participant F as Facilitator\n140|    participant M as Meta backend\n141|    A->>P: inference request\n142|    P-->>A: 402 + payment requirements\n143|    A->>W: sign EIP-3009 (within daily cap)\n144|    A->>P: retry + X-Payment\n145|    P->>F: verify + settle USDC\n146|    F-->>P: settled\n147|    P->>M: forward to Meta backend\n148|    M-->>A: inference streams\n149|    Note over A,P: ANY failure → speech continues, receipt \"unpaid\"\n150|```\n151|\n152|## 8. Scaling & bottlenecks (named, per framework step 5)\n153|\n154|| Load level | Bottleneck | Fix | Cost |\n155|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n156|| Demo day | TTS cold start on Akash | prewarm + keepalive + replaceable TTS interface | one GPU idling |\n157|| Demo day | serial STT→LLM→TTS latency | sentence-level streaming pipeline; TTS starts on first sentence | engineering time |\n158|| Demo day | Solana public RPC rate limits | dedicated RPC (Helius free tier) | zero |\n159|| Viral | per-character state growth | memory graph per character; roots batched across characters into one daily commit | storage |\n160|| Viral | inference cost per user | character's own x402 wallet funds itself — the business model IS the scaling answer | — |\n161|| Long-term | context staleness in big windows | structured memory graph over transcript stuffing (Kun: stale auto-memory is a liability) | — |\n162|\n163|## 9. Validation protocol (Kun gates — binding)\n164|\n165|1. **REQ tables below are human-authored intent.** Muse Code implements; it may not edit REQs. A failing REQ test means the *code* is wrong, by construction.\n166|2. **E2E over unit:** the binding suite is a scripted **judge simulation** (play the 180s storyboard headlessly) run on every merge to `main`.\n167|3. **Adversarial review per task:** AdaL reviews every Muse Code diff against the REQ table with author/reviewer isolation before merge. High-stakes surfaces (wallet policy, oracle gate, receipt mint) get the deepest review.\n168|4. **Two-rehearsal rule (Q17):** every demo beat passes twice consecutively, on the record, before submission.\n169|5. **Evidence honesty (bounded-payments rule):** no fabricated outputs. Every claim in the README maps to a reproducible artifact: tx link, log, or video timestamp. Unverified claims are labeled unverified.\n170|\n171|## 10. Atomic requirements\n172|\n173|### UC-1 `initialize_character` (signer: Owner)\n174|| REQ | The program shall | Test |\n175|| --- | --- | --- |\n176|| REQ-01 | Create one character config PDA with seeds `[\"character\", owner, character_id]` | Address derives from those seeds, canonical bump |\n177|| REQ-02 | Mint exactly one Metaplex Core asset as the character identity | Asset exists, owner = owner wallet |\n178|| REQ-03 | Attach the Attributes plugin with the genesis trait vector | Attributes readable on-chain |\n179|| REQ-04 | Attach the Oracle plugin gating `evolve_traits` to the runtime signer | Non-oracle mutation rejected |\n180|| REQ-05 | Mint exactly one Token-2022 non-transferable receipt to the owner | Transfer attempt fails |\n181|| REQ-06 | Reject duplicate `character_id` for the same owner | Second init fails |\n182|| REQ-07 | Set life stage to `born`, memory epoch to 0 | Read config |\n183|\n184|### UC-2 `commit_memory_root` (signer: Runtime signer)\n185|| REQ | The program shall | Test |\n186|| --- | --- | --- |\n187|| REQ-10 | Append `(epoch, root, timestamp)` to the character's root history account | History grows by one |\n188|| REQ-11 | Reject a signer that is not the runtime signer | Forged signer fails |\n189|| REQ-12 | Reject a duplicate or regressed epoch | Replay fails |\n190|| REQ-13 | Emit an event carrying the root | Event parseable by the indexer |\n191|\n192|### UC-3 `evolve_traits` (signer: Runtime signer, oracle-gated)\n193|| REQ | The program shall | Test |\n194|| --- | --- | --- |\n195|| REQ-20 | Apply a validated trait delta to the Attributes plugin | Explorer shows new traits |\n196|| REQ-21 | Reject any direct owner or third-party mutation | Both fail |\n197|| REQ-22 | Record the dream-cycle journal hash that motivated the mutation | Hash stored, linkable to off-chain journal |\n198|\n199|### UC-4 `crank_heartbeat` (permissionless)\n200|| REQ | The program shall | Test |\n201|| --- | --- | --- |\n202|| REQ-30 | Advance life stage only when its on-chain precondition holds | Early crank fails |\n203|| REQ-31 | Pay the crank caller from the vault PDA | Caller balance increases |\n204|| REQ-32 | Change no state when the precondition fails | Account diffs empty |\n205|\n206|### UC-5/6 Agent runtime (voice + vision)\n207|| REQ | The system shall | Test |\n208|| --- | --- | --- |\n209|| REQ-40 | Deliver first audio p50 < 2.5s warm | Latency harness, 20-turn run |\n210|| REQ-41 | Answer with the locked VoxCPM2 voice seed | Seed constant in config; two runs match timbre |\n211|| REQ-42 | On diarization ambiguity, greet as stranger and continue | Injected ambiguity → stranger greeting |\n212|| REQ-43 | Capture vision ONLY on explicit trigger | No frames leave without a trigger event |\n213|| REQ-44 | Store every observation with provenance (frame hash, mask, timestamp) | Record fields present |\n214|\n215|### UC-4 Memory + verification\n216|| REQ | The system shall | Test |\n217|| --- | --- | --- |\n218|| REQ-50 | Version memory records; corrections supersede, never delete | Correction yields v2, v1 retained |\n219|| REQ-51 | Produce a valid inclusion proof for any committed memory | Proof verifies against on-chain root |\n220|| REQ-52 | Fail verification loudly for a tampered memory | Modified byte → proof fails |\n221|\n222|### UC-7 Private memory challenge (Arcium MXE) — added 2026-10-28, ratified as MUST-HAVE by Tolu\n223|| REQ-53 | Answer a challenge about a memory's content via an Arcium MXE computation over encrypted memory shares, never exposing plaintext to any single node | MXE callback returns signed boolean; no plaintext in any node, log, or account |\n224|| REQ-54 | Record the signed challenge result on-chain, linked to the memory epoch and root | Result account exists, signature verifies against the MXE/cluster |\n225|| REQ-55 | Fail a challenge loudly on tampered memories or MXE protocol fault (abort semantics) | Tamper → loud failure; fault → explicit error state, no silent pass |\n226|\n227|### UC-6 Payment\n228|| REQ | The system shall | Test |\n229|| --- | --- | --- |\n230|| REQ-60 | Never block or delay speech on payment state | Facilitator killed mid-demo → speech continues |\n231|| REQ-61 | Enforce the daily spend cap on the character key | Cap+1 request refused |\n232|| REQ-62 | Log every receipt (paid/unpaid) to the life page | Receipt list grows |\n233|\n234|### Privacy + evidence\n235|| REQ | The system shall | Test |\n236|| --- | --- | --- |\n237|| REQ-70 | Store zero raw media/transcripts on-chain | On-chain account audit |\n238|| REQ-71 | Show model identity + turn cost in the UI | UI snapshot |\n239|| REQ-72 | Ship a redacted Muse Code audit log in `audit/` | Log present, secrets scan clean |\n240|| REQ-73 | README maps every claim to a reproducible artifact | Claim→proof matrix complete |\n241|\n242|## 11. Diagram → requirements traceability (bounded-payments discipline)\n243|\n244|Every node and animated journey in the canonical diagram (D1, rendered as `site/diagram.html` via glowmotion; static `architecture-overview.svg`) is governed by a REQ cluster. A diagram element with no REQs is decoration and gets deleted; a REQ with no diagram element is invisible scope and gets reviewed.\n245|\n246|| Diagram element | Journey / flow | Governing REQs |\n247|| --- | --- | --- |\n248|| Browser App ↔ LiveKit ↔ Muse Voice Transcribe | J1 voice turn (sync) | REQ-40, REQ-42 |\n249|| Spark Brain ↔ VoxCPM2 | J1 voice turn (sync) | REQ-40, REQ-41, REQ-71 |\n250|| Browser App → SAM 3.1 → Memory Graph | \"look at this\" | REQ-43, REQ-44, REQ-70 |\n251|| Brain ↔ Memory Graph → Merkle Batcher → Anchor `commit_memory_root` | J2 memory lineage (async) | REQ-10..13, REQ-50..52 |\n252|| Dream Scheduler → `evolve_traits` → Core asset | dream cycle (async) | REQ-20..22, D10 |\n253|| Anchor `initialize_character` → Core asset + Token-2022 receipt | birth | REQ-01..07 |\n254|| `crank_heartbeat` | heartbeat | REQ-30..32 |\n255|| Brain → x402 Paywall → Facilitator → Meta API | J3 self-payment | REQ-60..62, D4 |\n256|| Baseten Spark Open → Memory Graph | consolidation (async) | D7, D10 |\n257|| Muse Image → Core asset | portrait evolution (async) | D13, REQ-22 |\n258|| Life Page → Core asset / Wallet reads | verification surface | REQ-51, REQ-71, REQ-73 |\n259|| Trust boundary (diagram band 5 label) | — | REQ-70, D2, §5 |\n260|\n261|## 12. Setup readiness — can every REQ cluster actually be executed?\n262|\n263|| REQ cluster | Depends on | Status 2026-10-26 | Blocking action |\n264|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n265|| REQ-01..32 (Solana) | Anchor CLI, devnet SOL, Metaplex + Token-2022 programs | ✅ ready (Turbin3 stack proven in bounded-payments + cohort) | none |\n266|| REQ-40..44 (voice/vision) | Meta Model API key, LiveKit server, VoxCPM2 on Akash GPU | 🟡 credits claim pending; Akash SDL modeled on akashvisionagent | claim credits (Day 0) |\n267|| REQ-50..52 (memory/verify) | off-chain store + Merkle lib | ✅ ready (pure software) | none |\n268|| REQ-60..62 (x402) | Base Sepolia USDC, facilitator endpoint, character key | 🟡 faucet + facilitator pick on Day 7 | none yet (correctly sequenced late) |\n269|| REQ-70..73 (privacy/evidence) | repo hygiene, Muse Code audit export | 🟡 Muse Code installed on VPS (v1.4.13 verified); **bubblewrap missing — one sudo fix** | `sudo apt install -y bubblewrap` |\n270|| Harness | Muse Code on Linux | ✅ binary installs and runs; sandbox needs bubblewrap (see note) | the one-liner above |\n271|\n272|**Muse Code on Linux (open item RESOLVED 2026-10-26):** Linux is a first-class platform — the installer drops a native `muse` binary on `~/.local/bin`; v1.4.13 confirmed running on this VPS (Ubuntu 24.04 glibc). One critical nuance from the compiled notes: the sandbox is a bundled bubblewrap helper and Muse Code **refuses shell commands without it**. This VPS has `apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1` and no bubblewrap — fix: `sudo apt install -y bubblewrap` (the packaged bwrap is setuid and works despite the AppArmor restriction), then verify `bwrap --ro-bind / / true`. Auth: browser sign-in on the Mac, or `META_API_KEY` for headless VPS runs. The doer harness can therefore live on EITHER machine.\n273|\n274|## 13. Claim→proof matrix (Q17 skeleton — fill during build)\n275|\n276|| Claim | User-visible proof | Technical proof | Fallback | Owner | Status |\n277|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n278|| It remembers | recall beat in video | memory record + timestamp | prerecorded | Tolu | ☐ |\n279|| Interaction changes it | traits diff on explorer | Attributes before/after | screenshot pair | Tolu | ☐ |\n280|| History is provable | \"Verify\" button | Merkle proof vs on-chain root | recorded run | Tolu | ☐ |\n281|| It pays for itself | wallet balance ticking | x402 receipts on Base | tx links | Tolu | ☐ |\n282|| Built with Muse Code | `audit/` logs | sanitized session log | — | Tolu | ☐ |\n283|\n284|## 14. Stretch registry (cut by default — D14)\n285|\n286|| Stretch | Gate to uncut | Kill signal |\n287|| --- | --- | --- |\n288|| CCIP root mirror to Base (starter kit Example 02, TS SDK) | Days 1–7 green + 2 rehearsals done | any MUST item yellow |\n289|| ERC-8004 registry entry | CCIP already shipped | any MUST item yellow |\n290|| Chainlink-for-Agents data purchases | x402 core stable | any payment flakiness |","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a181da-48ac-7a10-94db-cf9f7c3d1a1f"},"kind":"task","run_id":"01a181d9-de31-70b2-80c6-58ffe0a281a4","task_id":"01a181da-48ac-7a10-94db-cf9f7c3d1a1f"}}
